{"path": "frontier/iterations/i130-spectral-harmonic-discovery.md", "sha256": "685b176ca930de9193b969dd236d8e0e76fcca7a27e926a71799ad2016f99fef", "bytes": 34411, "start": 98, "end": 145, "total_lines": 201, "passage_sha256": "2489954c06b2002ad3293bd02b38b5df46aae00e798f9f6f26985c3cdb23f5db", "ending": "For completeness, the exact-transfer and matching operations do not require a single common target k for all labels. Whole-ball restriction is a positive, mean-preserving L² contraction; freezing on the finite smooth frame is `O(η log(1/η)+η²)=o(η^(3/4))`, η(t)=t^(−3/4). A protected outer gap gives an invariant high-mode graph V_j=O(η_j^(3/4)); the finite relative inverse is paid by choosing J after τ_*>0. The exact low outward matrix is diagonal plus O(η^(3/4)). Simple crossings have signed first-order coefficients. Stable scalar Green sums are O(η⁻¹ᐟ²), giving trial coordinates O(η¹ᐟ⁴) inside the η¹ᐟ⁸ boxes, with strictly signed mismatch on opposite control faces. Noncrossing pairs use the geometrically convergent stable sum. The product-topology fixed point sets every mismatch to zero simultaneously; all p columns form a basis. None of these steps uses m_i<k, which enters only the last growth bound.", "convention": "UTF-8 splitlines; joined LF; no appended LF"}
